      "snippet": {
        "text": "The study by Kasneci et al. ( 2023) [111] examined the potential benefits of ChatGPT for enhancing student learning and supporting teachers' work.Kohnke et al. [143] investigated the possibilities of ChatGPT, a generative AI chatbot, for teaching and learning languages.In addition to demonstrating its benefits, they highlighted ChatGPT's controversy and limitations.In their conclusion, they outline the digital competencies required to use this chatbot in an ethical and efficient way to support language acquisition for both instructors and students.Using artificial intelligence, Henriksen et al. [112] demonstrate that three obstacles to classroom learning can be overcome: enhancing transfer, dispelling the illusion of explanation depth, and teaching students how to critically assess explanations.Opera et al. [144] reviewed the literature on artificial intelligence as it relates to education.One of the recommendations made by the researchers was that ChatGPT's responses should be cited and referenced.According to [112], ChatGPT can enhance student learning.As Mollick & Mollick [113] suggest, AI can support five strategies that improve student learning when used carefully and purposefully.Through diverse explanations and analogies, students are able to rectify widespread misconceptions and participate in low-stakes quizzes to help them comprehend difficult and abstract concepts.A comprehensive and careful white paper was created by academics from five German institutions by Gimpel et al. (2023) [114].Table 3 presents an analysis of how ChatGPT can be employed to bolster student learning, detailing various strategies and methods that have been found to be effective.The response provided by ChatGPT was pertinent and correct.The resource may be utilized as a self-study aid and rapid reference [115] Summarising Information\n\nLong articles or news stories may be dynamically summarized using AI, making it simpler for readers to rapidly understand the main ideas of a piece of media [116] Learning Mathematics This study's findings suggest several research directions to ensure the safe and thoughtful inclusion of chatbots, particularly ChatGPT, in math education [168] Facilitating collaboration\n\nThe ChatGPT program has the potential to be used as a tool for creating various scenarios where students collaborate to solve issues and accomplish objectives [117] Assessment Concept checking and exam preparation",
