on problems. In a missing-value problem, there are four quantities, three of which are provided, while the fourth is unknown. To solve the problem, the reader must reason multiplicatively to determine the missing value. While being able to solve such problems is important, the procedural ability to solve a missing value problem does not itself indicate that a student has a deep understanding of proportionality.",
