      "snippet": {
        "text": "However, the fact that it prepares the question by describing the shape itself was considered an aspect that could be improved. In this sense, it was considered that it would be difficult to prepare achievement tests for mathematics, especially geometry (where there are many shapes), with ChatGPT. However, this situation can be overcome with self-renewing artificial intelligence technology. ChatGPT4, a paid version, stands out with its shape creation and interpretation features (Lear, 2024). In addition, some studies found that ChatGPT4 performs better mathematically than ChatGPT 3.5 (Frieder et al., 2024). This situation shows that better quality results can be obtained with less intervention in future studies in mathematics education with artificial intelligence. In the study, the free version that teachers, students, and researchers can easily access was tested. \n\nThe use of artificial intelligence in educational studies has become widespread today. There are studies that show learning through artificial intelligence receives positive feedback from students who feel that artificial intelligence increases communication in learning (Kim et al., 2020), while there are other studies that showartificial intelligence does not provide reliable and stable support to the student in the reasoning process (Urhan et al., 2024). With this study, the adequacy of Chat-GPT in developing achievement tests in education was determined. The study showed that there was a need for some improvements in creating achievement tests with ChatGPT, an artificial intelligence tool. The test showed that by writing the target to be measured by artificial intelligence, multiple-choice questions suitable for that target could be written without intervention or with a few interventions. Giving clear and practical instructions is essential to prepare high-quality questions (Lee et al., 2024). It was observed that the number of interventions produced by the questions decreased depending on the shortness and clarity of the prompts given in the study. To obtain the desired answer from the generative artificial intelligence tools, linguistic skills and the detection of creative expressions are important. Therefore, determining the prompts that will reduce the number of interventions will increase the efficiency of using artificial intelligence in measurement and evaluation in mathematics education. It is a fact that creating a test with interventions in ChatGPT takes less time than creating a test from scratch.",
