      "snippet": {
        "text": "GPT-3 is trained on large amounts of data and recognizes as well as analyzes patterns and relationships within this data to generate coherent, context-dependent output (Floridi & Chiriatti, 2020). \n\nThe GPT-4 model, published by OpenAI (2023), can be accessed through the ChatGPT interface. GPT-4 achieved significantly high scores in the SAT Math Test: 700 out of 800 points (OpenAI, 2023). Experiences show that this LLM can be used in a variety of ways in the field of natural language processing, such as summarizing and translating texts or answering questions (Hadi et al., 2023;Ope-nAI, 2023). Further applications and developments can be seen in the ChatGPT interface: The DALL•E 3 text-to-image model can already generate images within the interface (Schorcht et al., 2024a). Possibly, OpenAI's text-to-video model Sora will enable the generation of audio-visual content. Another new development within OpenAI's catalog is the design of specialized AI agents (GPTs) based on individual instructions and resources. These specialized AI agents are designed to provide answers based on supplementary information. Following an idea proposed by Qian et al. (2023) in the software development field, these AI agents were linked together in an agent network, in order to master challenging tasks together in the role of various experts. In this study, we aim to contribute to a better understanding of AI support in education by revealing the potentials and challenges of using an agent network for mathematics educational contexts. \n\nIn the following section, we begin elaborating on the theoretical background by describing the role and definition of task design as well as the concept of multi-professional teams from the perspective of mathematics education. We go on to connect task design with AI explaining possible challenges like AI's black-box problem and introducing the idea of AI agents as a multi-professional team to support teachers in task design. The study design is presented and structured by introducing an overarching research question and two subordinate ones. The third section (\"Materials and methods\") presents the materials and methods of the study and subsequently describes the data collection, data material, and data analysis.",
